A structural risk is recorded:** the web app ships one `index` chunk with no route-level code splitting (`router.tsx` has no `lazy`), and every FE task grows it. W14 grew it from 1,610,006 to 1,787,510 bytes (+11 %), and every page load and new browser context parses all of it. **Decided:**<br>- the timeout is not raised;<br>- an FE repair task adds route-level code splitting and measures the bundle and the journey time before and after;<br>- the merged-tree e2e evidence is taken with W15, with no agent running (D-112).<br>**Practice:** the orchestrator never checks out, installs or builds in the dedicated tree while a review or audit run is active (D-082). With implementer runs active, a checkout or install there is listed in a run's `external_config_changed` only if it changes a configuration surface, as worktree creation does (D-100), and the orchestrator reviews any such entry. FE-R1's run, during which the A/B and a verification ran in that tree, lists none. | handbacks `T-DG4-ARCH-R2-solution-architect.md`, `T-DG4-BE-M3-backend-workflow-engineer.md`, `T-DG4-KBE-G2-kpi-benefits-engineer.md`, `T-DG4-FE-D-frontend-ux-engineer.md`; merges `801b9b6`, `38cc4d0`, `d72976c`; evidence `docs/delivery/test-evidence/DG4/orchestrator/w14-merged-d72976c/` | — |
