nd repeated a row; those lists now page by the time-ordered id.<br>Carried forward: a meeting action's My Work item does not follow later edits that go through `raid/actions.ts`, for BE-R3; `meeting-actions.ts` copies `createLinkedAction` because governance may not depend on `raid`, for ARCH-R2 to decide.<br>**BE-M2.** Four Modular-entry operations and the D-106 (e) precondition: a Modular G3 with its criteria met but no baseline and no outcome link answers 422 `gate.modular_links_missing`, and 201 once both are supplied. **End-to-End byte identity is proven:** 21 End-to-End G1–G4 responses (refusals, submissions, decisions, the gate list) were recorded with BE-M2's `gates.ts` and with the base commit's, normalized only for ids, instants and hashes, and are byte-identical. Two as-built deviations from ADR-0038 §7.4 are accepted and given to ARCH-R2 for the text:<br>- the precondition runs after the criteria check, because the DG2-approved `dg2-repairs.test.ts:461` must keep `gate_criteria_incomplete`;<br>- it applies to G3 only, as D-106 (e) says.<br>**Decided: the waiver half of 'rejected until supplied or waived'** (REQ-PB-005, REQ-S03-005). It cannot be reached through the API today: a `gate_exception` must cover one of G3's five criteria and none is about baselines or links, and the DG3 dispensation route refuses a waiver for a Modular transformation (`dispensation.waiver_requires_end_to_end`). BE-M2 correctly declined to count an unrelated G3 exception as a waiver, which would skip a control nobody waived. Of its three options, the orchestrator takes **(a), a narrow reopen of the DG3 dispensation route:** a G3 `waiver` becomes allowed on a Modular transformation **only** for the Modular-links precondition, and every other DG3 dispensation response and every End-to-End response stays byte-identical. This follows the D-089 Q2 and D-106 pattern.<br>- Rejected (b), a new G3 criterion: it changes every G3 criteria list, End-to-End included.<br>- Rejected (c), links only: it leaves the requirement text half met.<br>ARCH-R2 specifies the waiver (ADR-0021, ADR-0038), and a later backend task implements it and must prove the byte identity.<br>**Merge edits:** union only; media-type pin `[315, 314, 1]` = 304 + 9 BE-F2 + 2 BE-M2; 19 P4 mappers each defined and called once, no duplicate case label, no section after a dangling `case`.<br>**Merged-tree verification** (`affffce`): every check exit 0; unit 2352 + 259/2 in both locale settings (2342 + 10 BE-M2); integration 1661/1661 (1587 + 7 KBE-R2 + 22 BE-R2 + 29 BE-F2 + 16 BE-M2); e2e 228 passed. | handbacks `T-DG4-{BE-R2,BE-F2,BE-M2}-backend-workflow-engineer.md`, `T-DG4-KBE-R2-kpi-benefits-engineer.md`; merges `abc3bf4`, `d812d92`, `dc4ace1`, `affffce` | — |
