aReview`, and any later case), the worker gets its own implementation, or both use a pure `packages/shared` helper, with a parity test proving both paths write the same rows (the `createWorkItemOnce` precedent).<br>3. **REQ-S16-020 entity-group test split:** BE-H2 owns `adoption/entity-group.test.ts` (StakeholderGroup, AdoptionIntervention, training and assessment records); KBE-F adds the AdoptionMetricLink case in its own file, since the two run concurrently.<br>**Carried forward** (repair work or reviewer points, not accepted as done): BE-F's `governance.meeting_series_generate` has no `job_schedule` row and BE-I's benefit `control_cadence` has no `weekly` value, so both need repair-range migrations, to be allocated with BE-K's `0059`; the codes BE-F and BE-I added outside ADR-0032/0034 need architect acceptance and translations; transformation-scoped users cannot list reporting periods (FE-B); there is no workspace entry to the KPI screens; work items do not follow their source's due-date or owner changes (BE-D, BE-D2, BE-H); BE-I's closure fixture disables `closure_record_guard` as schema owner for one transaction, until BE-J's closure exists (code-security review).<br>**Merged-tree verification** (`19094f3`), every check exit 0: unit 2258 + 259/2 skipped in both locale settings (2208 + 23 BE-F + 27 FE-B); integration 1283/1283 (1199 + 24 BE-H + 20 BE-I + 40 BE-F); e2e 212 passed (en + ar; FE-B's two fixes included, since FE-B had re-run only the P4 specs). | handbacks `docs/delivery/handbacks/DG4/T-DG4-{BE-H,BE-I,BE-F}-backend-workflow-engineer.md`, `T-DG4-FE-B-frontend-ux-engineer.md`; merges `76c372a`, `6f046b1`, `ed795fa`, `19094f3` | — |
