| D-094 | 2026-10-09 | delivery-orchestrator | **BE-B integrated. The REQ-S10-003 literal 403 is accepted as a narrow reopen, and a small follow-up task, BE-B2, is scheduled.** `T-DG4-BE-B` (`75738e4`) delivered groups, role mappings, delegations (loop guard, 'B on behalf of A'), the P4 approval record (four outcomes, SoD, stale 409) and the escalation timer. All 23 operations are routed. Integration passed 892/892; first-run failures are disclosed.<br>**(1) REQ-S10-003.** Its acceptance text is: 'A12: an ADM-only user calling a gate or Finance approval endpoint gets 403'. As built, an ADM-only caller has no `transformation.read` and gets **404** from the DG1–DG3 gate-decision and baseline-validation endpoints. **Decision:** apply one narrow rule to those endpoints: a caller whose every grant in the organization is a technical-admin role gets 403 instead of 404. Every other caller's response is unchanged. This is a reopen of DG1–DG3 responses, scoped exactly as REQ-S10-003 requires, the D-089 Q2 pattern.<br>**(2) Schema need.** Two `work_item_kind` rows are needed for inbox reminders: `approval_outcome` and `approval_overdue` (ADR-0026 §4/§6). Migration `0058` (repair range) is assigned for them.<br>**(3) Scheduled follow-up.** `T-DG4-BE-B2` (backend-workflow-engineer) does (1) and (2): it writes `0058` and adds the reminder calls in `decideApproval` and `escalateOne`.<br>**(4) Accepted interpretations** (BE-B handback §4.4):<br>- a delegate must itself hold `approval.decide`;<br>- a deferral replaces the assignee's dated task;<br>- a resubmit keeps the assignee and the due date;<br>- an escalation routing-error row records `level + 1`;<br>- the extra refusal codes, which FE-A translates. | `docs/delivery/handbacks/DG4/T-DG4-BE-B-backend-workflow-engineer.md` | A reviewer reads S10-003 differently, or BE-B2 finds the narrow rule affects another caller. |
