| D-089 | 2026-10-09 | delivery-orchestrator | **The P4 plan is adopted, and the orchestrator decides its ten open questions and four reopen candidates as the architect recommended.** `T-DG4-ARCH-00` produced `docs/architecture/p4-plan.md`. It maps all 137 DG4 requirements, each to exactly one slice; the orchestrator checked that none is missing and none is duplicated. It also gives:<br>- the slice dependency graph;<br>- the 22 DG1–DG3 seams;<br>- 8 architecture tasks (ADR-0025 to ADR-0038; migrations `0028`–`0057`, with `0058`–`0069` held for repairs; lock classes from 730224);<br>- 30 implementer tasks in 11 waves of at most 4 runs.<br>**Decisions** (p4-plan §6; each slice ADR states the documented reason):<br>- **Q1.** The KPI aggregation rule is required on activation and on every P4 use, **not on create**. The DG2 create stays unchanged, so this is additive.<br>- **Q2 (reopen, accepted).** A gate submission may carry a mandatory criterion that is `incomplete` only when an accepted, unexpired waiver covers it, and the snapshot records the waiver. The `0017` CHECK becomes 'complete or covered'. Every DG2 refusal without a waiver is unchanged. REQ-S04-012 requires this.<br>- **Q3.** Delegation (REQ-S10-010) applies to the new P4 approvals and the existing ADR-0015 one-hop paths. The P3 approvals stay in person, with the DG3 422 kept. No reopen.<br>- **Q4.** G6 approval does not close a transformation. Closure is a separate governed action: an approved G6, plus validated value or a documented transition decision.<br>- **Q5.** RAID codes are `R-nn`, `A-nn` and `I-nn`. A dependency keeps its `DEP-nn` code.<br>- **Q6.** 'Next SteerCo' is the next scheduled Executive SteerCo meeting, or Unknown. 'Urgent route' is a configured number of working days, with a reason. 'Per release plan' is the linked milestone's approved date, or Unknown.<br>- **Q7.** The escalation chain is per T11 row; the default is the Approve role, then SP. An unmapped authority is a visible routing error.<br>- **Q8.** Cut-off dates are configuration. Automatic agenda generation is DG5 (REQ-S12-015).<br>- **Q9.** Single-actual entry with evidence. Bulk import is P6.<br>- **Q10.** A canonical `approval` table serves the new P4 approval types, with a read-only union view. Existing approval tables are not migrated.<br>- **Seam 15 (text change, accepted).** The closure-refusal clause 'which is not available in this release' becomes untrue and is corrected.<br>- **R1 (DG2 ADR doc defect).** ADR-0015 §2 says the gate engine writes `gate.submitted` and `gate.decided` outbox events, but as built it writes none. P4 implements them (ARCH-07), and the ADR sentence is corrected then.<br>- **R2/R3.** Performance areas and the sustainment entities (whose groups close at DG5) are built as increments in DG4.<br>- **R4.** Review assignments will state that DG4 rows citing later A-tests are judged on their own acceptance text.<br>The user may override any of these. | `docs/architecture/p4-plan.md`; `docs/delivery/handbacks/DG4/T-DG4-ARCH-00-solution-architect.md` | A slice architect finds a decision unworkable, or the user overrides one. |
